rdap — provenance note
=======================

Kept as a module-local NOTICE (same placement as the sibling `ocsp`/`dns`/
`whois` modules, which document the same live-capture reasoning).

Provenance
----------

rdap — clean-room implementation from RFC 7480-7484 and their RFC 9082/9083
renumbering (query URLs, response model, bootstrap). See `root.zig`'s
module doc comment; no third-party RDAP implementation's source or design
was consulted or copied.

`modules/rdap/src/goldens.zig` (added 2026-08-01) holds one real RDAP
domain response captured live from Public Interest Registry
(`rdap.publicinterestregistry.org`, via the `rdap.org` RFC 7484 bootstrap
redirect) for `iana.org` — see that file's own doc comment for the capture
recipe and what it exercises (ICANN's GDPR "redacted" extension, nested
entities, a missing top-level `handle`) that the hand-typed KATs in
`root.zig` do not.

Attribution for the captured response: NONE required, by the same reasoning
`ocsp`'s `NOTICE` gives for its live CA captures (root NOTICE §0's
black-box-oracle relationship): no third-party source or design was
consulted, only the observable JSON output of a public registry answering a
stock RDAP query over a public protocol (RFC 9082/9083) — protocol
structure plus facts (nameserver names, dates, a registrar name already
published in RDAP), not copyrightable expression. No root NOTICE change
accompanies this addition.

No GPL/LGPL/AGPL source was consulted or copied anywhere in this module.
